 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:29:21 -0700

smartclockmon (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Security: the exporter and the web view bounded nothing.  A
    request line with no newline grew memory at wire speed from one
    connection, and a connection that sent nothing held a thread for
    the life of the process.  Both now cap the request, the number in
    flight, and how long a client may take.  This matters for anyone
    serving the web view on anything but localhost.
  * The web view withholds the antenna position and the policy flags
    from its HTTP responses; it never displayed them, and it has no
    authentication of its own.
  * The web view no longer opens a daemon connection per request, which
    could take all sixteen of the daemon's client slots and lock out
    the monitor and the command line tool.
  * The chart latched into a zoom on every page load, which stopped the
    history updating; the "all" range fetched one hour rather than all
    of it; the hardware register showed as a bitmask rather than as the
    fault it names; the sky plot kept showing satellites after the
    daemon went away.
  * Clients time out after twenty seconds on a daemon that has stopped
    answering, rather than waiting for ever.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:15:11 -0700

smartclockmon (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * New: smartclock-web, a read-only browser view.  A polar sky plot, a
    live status strip, and history you can drag to zoom, with any two
    series on separate axes -- EFC against temperature being the one
    that earns its keep.  Serves on localhost only; the chart library
    is fetched from a CDN, pinned with an integrity hash.
  * smartclock-exporter and smartclock-web each ship a systemd unit and
    a conffile, both disabled until enabled.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Sun, 20 Sep 2026 23:10:12 -0700

smartclockmon (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * New: smartclock-exporter, Prometheus metrics served from the
    daemon's own readings, so a scrape costs the receiver nothing.  A
    reading the receiver declined is left out rather than exported as
    zero, and the age of each poll tier is exported so that a daemon
    which has stopped polling cannot pass for a steady oscillator.
  * The monitor's ASCII mode is gone: ratatui draws chart axes with
    box-drawing glyphs a caller cannot replace, so the fallback could
    never have been complete.
  * smartclock-cli --socket asks a running daemon instead of taking the
    serial port, so queries and diagnose work while logging continues.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Sun, 20 Sep 2026 22:46:20 -0700

smartclockmon (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * No change to the software.  Release and CI workflow only: a release
    now tells the APT repository to rebuild instead of waiting for its
    daily cron, the shared workflows are pinned, and neither is handed
    secrets it does not need.

